  "summary": "Adirondack is a rugged architectural style associated with the Great Camps within the Adirondack Mountains area in New York, United States.",
  "description": "Adirondack is a rugged architectural style associated with the Great Camps within the Adirondack Mountains area in New York, United States. These camps were built using native building materials and sited within an irregular wooded landscape. Camps for the wealthy were built to provide a primitive, rustic appearance while avoiding the problems of in-shipping materials from elsewhere.",
